※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4466

※ A tuple is several values travelling as one, and there is no tuple of none:
※ the brackets always hold at least one member, which the parser requires of a
※ tuple written out.  An array of no elements spread into a tuple leaves none,
※ and what a spread leaves obeys the same rule as what is written.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let empty: u8⟦0⟧ = ⟦⟧
    let nothing: 〈u8〉 = 〈⁂empty〉
    nothing⟦0⟧
